{"seq":1,"mint":"C3","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"The `Search` observation's label is the only part of a grep census that reaches a committed memo","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F2","F22","F27","F31"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"        buf.push(PendingEntry {\n            captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n            kind: ObservationKind::Search,\n            key: search_key(root_path, &m.root),\n            label: format!(\n                \"search: {root} (grep: {pattern}) — {files} file{} matched — {note}\",\n                if files == 1 { \"\" } else { \"s\" }\n            ),\n            output: String::new(),\n            world_root: m.root,\n            world_state: m.state,\n            pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n        });\n        for (file, matches) in by_file {\n            let m = world.for_path(Path::new(&file));\n            buf.push(PendingEntry {\n                captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n                kind: ObservationKind::GrepMatch,\n                key: resolve_key(Path::new(&file)),\n                label: format!(\"{file} (grep: {pattern})\"),\n                output: matches.join(\"\\n\"),\n                world_root: m.root,\n                world_state: m.state,\n                pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n            });\n        }","why":"A grep census records both a Search observation label and separate GrepMatch observation labels. The committed Facts renderer uses observation extent labels generically: `f.extent.iter().map(|e| e.label.as_str()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\"; \")`, so the assertion that only the Search label reaches a committed memo is incompatible with the captured implementation.","quoted":true}],"at":1790112034,"cost":0.006377548,"elapsed_ms":32717,"attempts":3,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":0}
